interface.longDescription:
MITA keeps your budget, expenses, recurring obligations and savings goals in your MITA account, so they are there in every future ChatGPT conversation.

In ChatGPT you can:
• record expenses in plain language — one at a time, several at once, or from a receipt photo you attach (ChatGPT reads the photo; MITA stores only the dates, amounts, categories and merchants, never the image);
• correct or delete an expense you recorded by mistake;
• tell MITA your monthly net income, currency, household size and savings target;
• preview a monthly budget that MITA builds with its deterministic rules from what you told it, and save it only after you have reviewed it;
• see where you stand against your budget, what you can spend per day, and how the month ends at your current pace;
• open your month as an interactive calendar right in the chat — each date's plan and spending, bills due and money set aside — and save it as an image;
• compare months and see up to twelve months of spending history and trends;
• add recurring expenses such as rent, and savings goals with a target date;
• send feedback to the MITA team.

MITA only works with the MITA account you sign in to — or create — on MITA's own page. MITA cannot initiate, execute or facilitate payments, money transfers or trades: it is not connected to your bank or payment accounts and does not hold money. MITA never invents figures: when it has no data for something, it says so. You can disconnect at any time in ChatGPT; changing your MITA password also ends ChatGPT's access.
